.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json

# Codex CLI local scratch (file or dir, depending on Codex version)
.codex

# /explain stages its printer-ready HTML here before the browser prints the PDF to the
# developer's chosen directory. It is staged IN-REPO because guard-repo-confinement.sh
# refuses every Write outside the repository; it is ignored because the report is a
# throwaway render of an answer, not a repository artifact.
.explain/

# Python bytecode for the skills' python helpers. It is a build artifact of the .py
# beside it, regenerated on every run — and a committed copy silently goes stale the
# moment its source is edited, which is exactly what had happened to the routine
# comparer's cache before it was removed.
__pycache__/

# /setup-routines and /workaholify stage the raw RemoteTrigger response here before
# reading it back. It is staged IN-REPO because guard-repo-confinement.sh refuses every
# Write outside the repository; it is ignored because it is a snapshot of an account, and
# a committed snapshot of live routines goes stale silently — the exact failure the
# "could not check" reporting exists to avoid.
.routines/

# VitePress site under docs/ — installed dependencies, build cache and build output
# are regenerated from docs/package.json and never committed.
docs/node_modules/
docs/.vitepress/cache/
docs/.vitepress/dist/

# Developer-maintained leak denylist for release-scan (client names must never ship)
.workaholic/leak-denylist

# Proposal batch's runner-local processed-commit cursor (/propose; never shared state)
.workaholic/proposal-cursor

# The /moderate tick log. It is an OPERATIONAL LOG, not knowledge, and since 2026-09-01
# (issue #782) it lives on its own branch — `moderate/scripts/log-ref.sh` — rather than on
# `main`. Measured before the move: ~50 commits a day, three per tick, the single largest
# author of `main`'s history, none of them a change to the development target.
#
# It is ignored rather than merely untracked, and that is the enforcement: an ordinary
# `git add -A` in a container that has just ticked cannot put the log back on `main` by
# accident. `log-append.sh` still writes here and every reader still reads here — only the
# destination of the commit moved. `step-open-log.sh` hydrates this directory from the log
# branch at the start of each tick, which is what keeps the dedup's memory across containers.
.workaholic/moderations/
